## What FBE.6 surfaced (foldback-reopening findings)

### BLOCKER-FBE6.1 — README/getting-started.md install flow broken

The README's literal install (`pip install -e framework/tools/loam`
followed by `loam init .`) FAILS at step 3 because `loam-init` is a
separate Python package not pulled in by installing
`framework/tools/loam` alone. A stranger following the README
literally gets `loam: error: argument subcommand: invalid choice:
'init' (choose from )` (exit code 2).

The actual working install path is `pip install -r install-from-
source.txt` (FBE.4 ratified this), but neither README.md nor docs/
getting-started.md mention `install-from-source.txt`. The supporting
doc `docs/install-from-source.md` exists but is only linked from the
install-from-source.txt header comment; the headline install flow in
README/getting-started.md still describes the broken single-component
install.

This is an ODD §2.5 violation: the README's documented contract
(install → loam init works) is not satisfied by the actual code path
the README describes. The install-from-source.txt mechanism IS
satisfied by the code path FBE.4 introduced — the docs just weren't
updated to point at it.

Fix shape: doc-edit amendment (FBE.8) updating README.md +
getting-started.md to point at `install-from-source.txt` as the
v0.1.0 entry point.

